{
	title: 'One authoritative subscription usage store',
	spec: 'Subscription quota has one authoritative host store, updated by every provider observation and every successful status endpoint read. /status refreshes each subscription when invoked rather than serving a one-minute cache. Session plans reference account data instead of copying usage windows. The host sends account usage updates to all connected clients, including idle tabs, and seeds the store on connection. Both terminal and web resolve plans from their one client master store. The browser uses the installed Solid 2 createStore and draft-first reconciliation so window field changes notify their consumers without copying quota into each tab or polling. Remove the redundant status-window cache. Preserve account selection and per-account separation, partial header merges, complete endpoint replacement, and full failures. Invariant restored: reading status updates master quota and all views of an account observe the same master values. Tests cover idle-client updates, status refresh, account isolation, and fine-grained Solid 2 reactions.',
