	notes: [
		'Session Plan carries only account slot/count and the provider-account key. usage.ts remains the authoritative persisted store; observation publishes per-account updates, and the initial tabs greeting seeds the client master store. Common connection applies updates before dispatch. Web installs the pinned Solid 2 createStore and reconciles fields with draft callbacks; quota events do not call app.changed. Terminal uses the same master lookup. /status refreshes even fresh subscriptions, preserves cached data with existing visible error advice on failure, and replaces complete endpoint windows. Learning an email rekeys master data and updates open session references.',
		'Solid 2 package resolution matters: Bun uses the server build, whose effects do not establish browser reactivity. Verify reactive behavior in Chromium instead. The existing compact-status browser regression now checks quota-only updates without Stats events, retained nodes and draft, and zero status mutations for an unrelated account at 320, 390, 1024 and 1600-pixel layouts. No extra browser polling or provider request is introduced by rendering; explicit /status reads query each subscription.',
